#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:4
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "簡介"

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:6
msgid ""
"The **Instrumentor** is a highly configurable instrumentation pass for LLVM-"
"IR that allows users to insert custom runtime function calls at various "
"program points. Unlike traditional instrumentation tools that are hardcoded "
"for specific purposes (like sanitizers or profilers), the Instrumentor "
"provides a flexible, configuration-driven approach where users can specify:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:12
msgid ""
"**What** to instrument (loads, stores, allocations, function calls, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:13
msgid "**Where** to instrument (before or after operations)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:14
msgid ""
"**What information** to pass to the runtime (pointers, values, sizes, types, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:15
msgid ""
"**Whether** to modify program behavior (replace values, redirect pointers, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:17
msgid ""
"The Instrumentor is designed to support a wide variety of use cases "
"including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:19
msgid "Custom memory profilers and trackers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:20
msgid "Performance analysis tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:21
msgid "Dynamic program analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:22
msgid "Debugging and tracing utilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:23
msgid "Stack usage monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:24
msgid "Custom sanitizers and checkers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Instrumentor.md:26
msgid ""
"To use the Instrumentor it is recommended to run the wizard script located "
"at `./llvm/utils/instrumentor-config-wizard.py`. The script will "
"interactively create a configuration file and a stub runtime which is "
"required to be linked into the instrumented program."
msgstr ""

